  "goodToKnow": "Die Optik is optics, the science of light: Jena is a historic centre of German optics, home of Carl Zeiss. In everyday speech, it means the look or appearance: eine schicke Optik, Laminat in Holzoptik (wood-look laminate). In politics, die Optik means how something looks to the public: Die Optik ist schlecht (it looks bad). Der Optiker is an optician, where Germans buy glasses. Optisch means visual."
